# HomeLab 3 - Adding a ticketing server.

Purpose - Create a ticketing system tied to my current AD lab set up


### Support Set Up
I mapped a shared network drive to easily share screenshots between multiple devices via Samba (my lab PC is Windows dualbooted on an old MacBook, my primary PC is Linux.) 


### Environment 
Ubuntu Server 26.04.1
osTicket 
PHP (8.5.4)
MariaDB
OracleVirtual Box with Bridged Networking (3 VM's total - each with 2GB RAM and 20GB disk space)

### Set Up

1 - Downloaded and spun up a VM of Ubuntu Server via Virtual Box 
2 - Set a static IP address for the Linux server for communication with the Active Directory Server
3 - Set up a host (A) record  on the AD DNS manager to point the hostname at the server's static IP, verified connection with nslookup
4 - Verified communication between VM's via ping
5 - Configured Firewall settings on the Linux server to enable SSH and http to ensure the ticketing site is reachable.

6 - Logged into the Linux Server from the Windows host via SSH. Downloaded the following packages to set up ticketing system: 
        -Apache - web server
        -Maria DB - data base server
        -PHP - programming language for osTicket (osTicket's current version documentation suggests PHP 8.2-8.4 - I downloaded 8.5 and it ran without issue,   save for one blank window that worked on page refresh.) 
        -libapache2-mod-php - module to connect Apache to PHP
        -php-mysql - driver to connect PHP to Maria DB

7 - Ran the secure installer on Maria DB
8 - Logged into Maria DB - created new 'osticket' database, and osticket_user (seperate from root to enforce principle of least privilege.) 
9 - After downloading osTicket with wget - I unzipped it and copied the application into Apache's web root (using sudo cp -R) in order to make it reachable via browser - then I gave Apache ownership of the entire folder using chown -R to allow the installer to write to the file.
10 - Opened osTicket from the browser and ran the installer successfully 

11 - Took recommended security hardening steps from the post-install screen
            -Deleted the set-up folder (using rm -r) to prevent the installer from running again with changed settings. 
            -Ran chmod 0444 to set the config file to read-only.       

12 - Logged into osTicket and created several fictional agents, with varying levels of privilege, as well as Help Topics for the drop downlist
13 - Accessed the user-side of osTicket to verify additions to dropdown list were successful and submitted a ticket. 
14 - Switched back to admin window to ensure successful ticket submission. 
15 - Logged in to third VM as a test user - submitted a ticket requesting a password reset.
16 - Received ticket on osTicket - prompted password reset on next logon via Active Directory, confirmed worked client-side and closed the ticket.


### Troubleshooting 
1 - Windows PC was unable to find the shared Samba folder from Linux PC | FIXED: There was a typo in the smb.conf file (a dash where an equals sign was needed)
2- SSH Login failed | FIXED: I forgot the syntax ssh username@logindestination 
3 - osTicket will not download via CLI Error 404 | FIXED: There was a typo in the link 
4 - osTicket downloaded the .git file instead of .zip | FIXED: I was using the wrong link! 
